  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The Padres couldn't score, couldn't stay ahead, and couldn't recover from the second inning onward.",
    "what_this_means": "They chased from the opening frame and never caught up. V\u00e1squez gave them four solid innings. The bullpen was clean after that, three pitchers combining for 3.1 scoreless. But the lineup managed five hits and eight strikeouts. Six runners reached base in scoring position. Zero of them scored. That's not close. That's not a game you win, and they didn't. They fell back 1.5 games in the division on a night when the pitching deserved better.",
    "what_to_watch": "This is what happens when the pitching holds and the offense doesn't answer. Wandy Peralta threw 1.2 clean. Yuki Matsui struck out two in 1.1 scoreless. Ron Marinaccio got through 1.2 without damage. The Dodgers scored four and held it. The Padres had their chances. Runners in scoring position three times in the first five innings. And did nothing with them. The game was decided the moment the fourth and fifth innings came and went empty. Now they've lost two straight and inconsistency is staring them in the face again.",
